cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this curriculum, its notebooks, experiments, or explanatory material in research or development work, please cite the repository and the specific release or commit used."
type: manual
title: "LLM Trainer Masterclass"
version: "0.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Hashemi"
    given-names: "Seyed Mohammad Abuzar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mahashemi/llm-training-mastercalss"
url: "https://github.com/mahashemi/llm-training-mastercalss"
abstract: "A free-first, research-oriented and implementation-heavy curriculum for understanding, building, training, evaluating, optimizing, deploying, and managing large language models. The project combines textbook chapters, 25-minute lectures, executable laboratories, runbooks, research reproduction guides, resource planning, and organizational and funding frameworks."
keywords:
  - large language models
  - LLM training
  - language model pretraining
  - fine-tuning
  - supervised fine-tuning
  - LoRA
  - QLoRA
  - data curation
  - evaluation
  - distributed training
  - multilingual models
  - low-resource languages
  - reproducibility
  - machine learning education
